SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia tis Trygis\, Propouli
LOCATION:Propouli\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Athonite metochi of Panagia tis Trygis ('of the Vintage') at Propouli in north-west Lemnos\, a chapel of 1706 with a rare icon of the Virgin in white\, is the island's main Dormition pilgrimage: services from the 13th\, liturgy and procession on the morning of the 15th\, vespers at 17:00\, served by monks of Simonopetra. Hundreds come from all over the island\; combine with Myrina's own Koimisis parish feast (14-15 August).\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#propouli-feast-of-panagia-tis-trygis-propouli
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#propouli-feast-of-panagia-tis-trygis-propouli
